> Membership in a selma'o may imply NOTHING about its semantics.

In principle, this is true. I made the same point myself to Xod the
other day, about zi'o being in KOhA. But it is a largely irrelevant
point, because usually membership of a selmaho does imply something
about a word's semantics. And when we are trying to work out what a
word means, the only thing that gets us beyond a complete vacuum is
its selmaho membership and its gloss.

I realize that you want us to insist on every aspect of meaning being
induced from usage. The best thing would you to place on the wiki
a statement of your ideological position, and then not participate
in discussions whose existence you disapprove.

> Membership
